# Vendored from conda-forge/clang-compiler-activation-feedstock

Fetched via `http get` from raw.githubusercontent.com at the pinned ref
(github.com/conda-forge/clang-compiler-activation-feedstock), not a
checked-out branch. Files kept: the activate/deactivate script pair,
build.sh (computes the FINAL_* flags and does the @VAR@ substitution),
install-clang.sh/install-clangxx.sh (canonical install step), the license,
and the variant config + meta.yaml for reference (values quoted into
render-install-osx.sh, not re-parsed at build time).

This lineage differs from ctng-compiler-activation (Linux): CHOST/CBUILD are
Apple triples (arm64-apple-darwin20.0.0 for osx-arm64 native), activation
runs through a single _tc_activation(act_nature, tc_prefix, ...) call per
script rather than ctng's shared helper + @C_EXTRA@/@CXX_EXTRA@ indirection,
and there is no separate binutils package — Apple's linker/ar/etc. come from
cctools_osx-arm64 + ld64_osx-arm64 (see the naga-acpp-clang_osx-arm64 run
deps in recipe.yaml).

render-install-osx.sh renders ONLY the osx-arm64 native slice (this
toolchain's only mac lane); build.sh's linux/osx-64/cross branches are not
ported. The ACPP delta (ACPP_TARGETS/ACPP_CLANG/ACPP_CPU_CXX on the clangxx
side) is applied as a second _tc_activation call appended after the
canonical one, not a template edit — the vendored files here stay faithful
copies.
